    "chunk_text": "Shipping is our future and the spin-off benefits that would come in as a result of that are, the logistics industry and the freight forwarding industry. I think those are not fully exploited as yet. You see, Singapore has grown by default. Owing to Sri Lanka\u2019s past civil disturbances, the lack of coherency, consistency and the policy adaptiveness being delayed, Singapore has been able to move forward. You see Dubai, on the other side, has taken advantage of it. Being between the Far East and the West, Sri Lanka could have played a pivotal role, but lost the opportunity to Fujairah. So, Dubai has taken the advantage of it before it moves to Europe.\n\nYou could see that the CICT is handling roughly around 2.3 million to 2.4 million containers when the potential is about 2.6 million to 2.7 million TEUs. So, we are full to the brim in terms of capacity there. Then, we have the JCT which should be handling about 2.6 million to 2.7 million TEUs, but we are just averaging around 2.0 million to 2.1 million TEUs. So, it is underperforming. Also, the productivity is something which we should be\n\n631 632\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dc4\u0dd4 \u0dcf\u0da0\u0dc3 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dda\u0dc1\u0dc0\u0dda \u0dba \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dbb]\n\n2019 \u0dc0\u0dd1\u0db4\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd1\u0db8\u0dca\u0dbb\u0dae\u0dd2 18"
