    "chunk_id": "2019-09-18-2019-09-18-0102",
    "chunk_index": 102,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "02cc69411021b63db059305daf2c3bf3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1342,
    "chunk_text": "You could see that the CICT is handling roughly around 2.3 million to 2.4 million containers when the potential is about 2.6 million to 2.7 million TEUs. So, we are full to the brim in terms of capacity there. Then, we have the JCT which should be handling about 2.6 million to 2.7 million TEUs, but we are just averaging around 2.0 million to 2.1 million TEUs. So, it is underperforming. Also, the productivity is something which we should be\n\n631 632\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dc4\u0dd4 \u0dcf\u0da0\u0dc3 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dda\u0dc1\u0dc0\u0dda \u0dba \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dbb]\n\n2019 \u0dc0\u0dd1\u0db4\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd1\u0db8\u0dca\u0dbb\u0dae\u0dd2 18\n\nIn the process, we find the delays that are taking place in the Port unbearable.\n\nInter-terminal operations are far too slow. I think we need to have a reality check into our shipping industry because a sense of inefficiency and lethargy has crept in, which needs to be corrected with immediate effect. The delays in inter-terminal transfers are so long that delays in handling ships are also taking place and that is a concern for the shipping industry. So, I think we need to ensure that this type of things are checked, looked at and corrected immediately. We need to have a professional team. If we are unable to discharge the services owing to lack of forethought or planning, let us ensure that efficiency is brought in so that we do not lose the opportunity that is before us."
  },
